## 🚀 Next.js Specific Considerations

### Server vs Client Components

**Server Components** (default):

```tsx
// app/page.tsx - Server Component
export default function HomePage() {
  return (
    <div style={{ backgroundColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)" }}>
      <ModusButtonDemo /> {/* Client Component */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Client Components** (for interactivity):

```tsx
// app/components/ModusButtonDemo.tsx - Client Component
"use client";

import { ModusWcButton } from "@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react";

export default function ModusButtonDemo() {
  return (
    <ModusWcButton
      color="primary"
      onButtonClick={() => console.log("Clicked!")}
    >
      Click me
    </ModusWcButton>
  );
}
```

### CSS Import Order

**Critical**: Modus icons CSS must come before Tailwind:

```css
/* app/globals.css */
@import url("https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@trimble-oss/modus-icons@1.17.0/dist/field-systems/fonts/modus-icons.css");
@import "tailwindcss";

/* Your styles here */
```

### TypeScript Integration

Ensure proper type declarations in `types/modus.d.ts`:

```typescript
declare namespace JSX {
  interface IntrinsicElements {
    "modus-wc-button": {
      color?: "primary" | "secondary" | "tertiary" | "warning" | "danger";
      variant?: "filled" | "outlined" | "borderless";
      size?: "xs" | "sm" | "md" | "lg";
      onButtonClick?: (event: CustomEvent) => void;
      children?: React.ReactNode;
    };
  }
}
```

## 🎨 Working with Colors in Practice

### Color Palette Reference

**Always reference the color palette page** at `/color-palette` to see all available colors and their proper usage. This page shows:

- ✅ **Visual color swatches** for all design system colors
- ✅ **CSS variable names** (e.g., `--primary`, `--destructive`)
- ✅ **Tailwind class names** (e.g., `bg-primary`, `text-destructive-foreground`)
- ✅ **Theme adaptation** - colors change automatically in light/dark themes
- ✅ **Usage examples** for both custom UI and Modus Web Components

### Loading States and Skeletons

**✅ CORRECT - Use Modus design system colors:**

```tsx
// Loading skeleton with proper Modus colors
if (!mounted) {
  return (
    <div className="max-w-6xl mx-auto p-8">
      <div className="animate-pulse">
        <div className="h-8 bg-muted rounded mb-8" />
        <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          {[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9].map((i) => (
            <div key={i} className="h-32 bg-muted rounded-lg" />
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

**❌ WRONG - Don't use hardcoded Tailwind colors:**

```tsx
// DON'T DO THIS - violates color rules
<div className="h-8 bg-gray-200 rounded mb-8" />
<div key={i} className="h-32 bg-gray-200 rounded-lg" />
```

